{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Day and night: Earth's rotation","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#1b2a41","font":"Verdana, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c1-i","picto":"globe"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"What causes day and night on Earth?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"Earth spinning on its axis","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"The sun going around the Earth","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"The moon blocking the sun","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Rotation"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Rotation is the spinning of the Earth around its own imaginary line called an axis. One full spin takes about 24 hours."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"How long does it take the Earth to spin once around?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"About 24 hours","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"About 12 hours","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"About 365 days","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c4-i","picto":"sun"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Why does the sun seem to move across the sky each day?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"The Earth is turning, so we face the sun, then turn away","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"The sun really travels around the Earth each day","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"The sun gets bigger and smaller each day","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"You are on a camping trip at dawn. The sky is turning gold. Do you watch the sun rise or check your map first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Watch the sun rise","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Check the map first","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You watch the sun climb. As the Earth turns, the sun seems to rise in the east. Keep watching."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The map shows east and west. Knowing the Earth turns from west to east helps you find the sunrise."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"In which direction does the sun appear to rise?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"East","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"West","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"North","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Day and night"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-e","content":"Day is when your part of the Earth faces the sun. Night is when it turns away from the sun."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"When it is day for us in Ireland, what is it doing on the far side of the world?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"It is night there","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"It is day there too","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"It is always sunset there","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You now know how day and night happen."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"The Earth spins once every 24 hours, and that spin brings us day and night and makes the sun seem to move across the sky."}],"actions":[]}}
